{"text": "It is worth pointing out. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That leaves do not drop to the ground. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Because they are dying. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Rather, the tree initiates an active process. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Of clever recycling called senescence. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> A tree, like an oak for example. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Would struggle to survive. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Through a harsh winter. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> If it retained its canopy of leaves. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> It would risk damage. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> From strong winter winds. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And would lose more water from its leaves. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Than it could draw up from the frozen ground. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> If it did not blow over it would die of thirst. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> As winter approaches. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The length of the day shortens. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The temperature drops. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And plants, including trees, can detect this change. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> It signals to them. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That it is time to lose their leaves. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> First, however, trees carefully suck. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> All of the useful nutrients out of the leaves. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And then, with surgical precision. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Block up that pathway into the leaves. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> That blocked pathway at the base of the leaf stem. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Creates a weakness. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And, in the wind, the leaves snap off. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> And fall to the ground.", "alignment": {"characters": ["I", "t", " ", "i", "s", " ", "w", "o", "r", "t", "h", " ", "p", "o", "i", "n", "t", "i", "n", "g", " ", "o", "u", "t", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "T", "h", "a", "t", " ", "l", "e", "a", "v", "e", "s", " ", "d", "o", " ", "n", "o", "t", " ", "d", "r", "o"